WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.368 --> 00:00:01.626
- Good morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:01.626 --> 00:00:05.355
Today's message is
choose who you listen to.

00:00:05.355 --> 00:00:07.284
Over to you, Gabrielle Union.

00:00:07.284 --> 00:00:09.294
(rooster crowing)

00:00:09.294 --> 00:00:12.023
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:12.023 --> 00:00:14.852
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:14.852 --> 00:00:18.352
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:22.834
- Early in my career, I was named

00:00:22.834 --> 00:00:24.578
the next it girl.

00:00:24.578 --> 00:00:27.997
And you're like, "Well, I think I should

00:00:27.997 --> 00:00:29.450
"really believe this."

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:32.084
You know, and then you read,
"You're the worst thing ever,

00:00:32.084 --> 00:00:33.523
"you should never leave the house."

00:00:33.523 --> 00:00:35.481
And you're like, oh, we
should throw that out.

00:00:35.481 --> 00:00:37.429
And eventually you just
kind of get to a place

00:00:37.429 --> 00:00:39.081
where they kind of cancel each other out.

00:00:39.081 --> 00:00:40.375
You're going to hear the naysayers

00:00:40.375 --> 00:00:41.455
and the people who think you suck,

00:00:41.455 --> 00:00:42.774
and there are going to
be the people who think

00:00:42.774 --> 00:00:45.560
you're the second coming of pockets,

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:48.844
but it's usually somewhere in the middle.

00:00:48.844 --> 00:00:53.099
If you believe all your
praise, there's nowhere to go,

00:00:53.099 --> 00:00:53.932
you're not going to grow.

00:00:53.932 --> 00:00:57.267
And if you believe every
negative thing about you,

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:58.754
you're not going to get out of bed.

00:00:58.754 --> 00:01:00.673
So, I try to be reasonable.

00:01:00.673 --> 00:01:04.170
People whose opinion I respect, I listen.

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:06.229
- You need to be really
careful who you listen to.

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:07.333
You've got this big dream,

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:08.621
you've got these big ambitions,

00:01:08.621 --> 00:01:10.686
you want to make your mark,
you want to do your thing,

00:01:10.686 --> 00:01:12.556
and often that's scary.

00:01:12.556 --> 00:01:14.075
You know, if it involves doing something

00:01:14.075 --> 00:01:16.660
you've never done before,
that can be quite scary,

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:19.294
and when people tell you
that you can't do it,

00:01:19.294 --> 00:01:20.863
when people tell you that you suck,

00:01:20.863 --> 00:01:22.852
when people tell you it's
never going to work out,

00:01:22.852 --> 00:01:24.708
a lot of times that's really hard to hear

00:01:24.708 --> 00:01:27.088
because you are doubting yourself.

00:01:27.088 --> 00:01:29.041
And when you hear that from other people,

00:01:29.041 --> 00:01:32.333
that just compounds the
doubt and makes you wonder,

00:01:32.333 --> 00:01:34.158
can I actually go out an do this thing?

00:01:34.158 --> 00:01:35.540
And so choosing who you listen to

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:36.886
is really, really important.

00:01:36.886 --> 00:01:39.424
Some people will pour rain on your parade

00:01:39.424 --> 00:01:40.999
because they're jealous,

00:01:40.999 --> 00:01:43.282
because maybe they've taken their shot

00:01:43.282 --> 00:01:46.195
at following their dreams
and it didn't work out,

00:01:46.195 --> 00:01:47.830
and so now nobody around them

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:49.339
can have success either.

00:01:49.339 --> 00:01:50.830
Nobody else is allowed to go off

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:53.400
and be an entrepreneur and
chase their dreams because

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:55.278
they tried it and it didn't work out,

00:01:55.278 --> 00:01:56.947
and so nobody else can have it.

00:01:56.947 --> 00:01:58.788
Life sucks, and they're going to drag

00:01:58.788 --> 00:02:00.763
everybody down in the hole with them.

00:02:00.763 --> 00:02:01.981
That's a lot of people.

00:02:01.981 --> 00:02:03.900
Others may rain on your parade because

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.356
they actually love you.

00:02:05.356 --> 00:02:07.177
They just don't see what you see.

00:02:07.177 --> 00:02:08.536
You know, your parents may think that

00:02:08.536 --> 00:02:09.416
it's not a great idea,

00:02:09.416 --> 00:02:11.181
or your guidance
counselor, or your friends

00:02:11.181 --> 00:02:13.852
may not think that what
you're doing is feasible,

00:02:13.852 --> 00:02:17.315
because in their world,
nobody's ever done it,

00:02:17.315 --> 00:02:19.182
because they haven't done it.

00:02:19.182 --> 00:02:22.488
And your parents may be
thinking success equals this,

00:02:22.488 --> 00:02:24.367
because that's what success is for them,

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:26.212
because that's the path that they took.

00:02:26.212 --> 00:02:28.207
And so they may be raining on your parade,

00:02:28.207 --> 00:02:30.325
but it's out of love,
it's not out of jealousy.

00:02:30.325 --> 00:02:33.123
At the end of the day, they want
to see you become successful,

00:02:33.123 --> 00:02:35.686
they just have a different
definition of success,

00:02:35.686 --> 00:02:38.599
and they don't want to
see you go through pain,

00:02:38.599 --> 00:02:41.533
and hurt, and struggle, and woes,

00:02:41.533 --> 00:02:43.886
and maybe not reaching your goal.

00:02:43.886 --> 00:02:45.104
And then there are other
people who will give you

00:02:45.104 --> 00:02:48.002
the perfect advice, exactly what you need

00:02:48.002 --> 00:02:50.074
exactly at the right
time that you need it.

00:02:50.074 --> 00:02:54.431
And so, really pay attention
to who is giving this advice,

00:02:54.431 --> 00:02:57.075
and not trying to have an
emotional reaction to it,

00:02:57.075 --> 00:02:58.295
but look at that person.

00:02:58.295 --> 00:03:01.139
Say, "Has this person
done what I want to do?

00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:03.307
"Does this person have the expertise

00:03:03.307 --> 00:03:05.147
"to give me the advice that I need?"

00:03:05.147 --> 00:03:06.435
Because if somebody is telling you

00:03:06.435 --> 00:03:09.684
that your idea sucks
and will never work out,

00:03:09.684 --> 00:03:13.120
and they haven't done
what you are trying to do,

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:15.873
then their advice is meaningless to you.

00:03:15.873 --> 00:03:17.674
If anything, you should do the opposite.

00:03:17.674 --> 00:03:20.453
Why are you taking advice
from someone who hasn't done

00:03:20.453 --> 00:03:22.382
what you want to do?

00:03:22.382 --> 00:03:25.267
You cannot let their limiting mindset

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:27.293
prevent you from being great.

00:03:27.293 --> 00:03:29.306
And it doesn't mean you
need to attack them.

00:03:29.306 --> 00:03:30.541
It doesn't mean you need to say,

00:03:30.541 --> 00:03:31.846
"You don't know what you're talking about!

00:03:31.846 --> 00:03:33.646
"You have a limiting mindset!

00:03:33.646 --> 00:03:36.555
"You've never gone out
and achieved your dreams!"

00:03:36.555 --> 00:03:39.157
You don't have to hurt them back,

00:03:39.157 --> 00:03:41.536
but you also don't have to react

00:03:41.536 --> 00:03:43.503
to the information they're giving you.

00:03:43.503 --> 00:03:46.761
Treat them like a child,
treat them like a puppy,

00:03:46.761 --> 00:03:48.693
treat them like a baby.

00:03:48.693 --> 00:03:49.992
They can't help it.

00:03:49.992 --> 00:03:51.787
They're negative.

00:03:51.787 --> 00:03:54.460
It may be out of jealousy,
it may be out of love,

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:57.662
but either way, you wouldn't
take advice from a baby.

00:03:57.662 --> 00:04:00.153
And if you can diffuse that in your head,

00:04:00.153 --> 00:04:02.543
if you can understand that these people

00:04:02.543 --> 00:04:04.767
have not done what you're trying to do,

00:04:04.767 --> 00:04:06.418
and not listen to their advice,

00:04:06.418 --> 00:04:08.152
and not listen to their doubts,

00:04:08.152 --> 00:04:11.710
and still know that you
need to get this done,

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:12.788
and maybe it doesn't work out,

00:04:12.788 --> 00:04:13.989
maybe you don't hit that dream,

00:04:13.989 --> 00:04:15.233
maybe you don't get your goals,

00:04:15.233 --> 00:04:16.816
but you still need to know.

00:04:16.816 --> 00:04:19.725
Because you would rather
fail and at least know

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:22.582
than live the rest of your life uncertain

00:04:22.582 --> 00:04:26.197
and in regret, wishing you had gave more

00:04:26.197 --> 00:04:29.097
to the cause to figure
out if it would work.

00:04:29.097 --> 00:04:32.512
Stop planning, stop
thinking with the head,

00:04:32.512 --> 00:04:34.927
stop using your logic all the time.

00:04:34.927 --> 00:04:39.699
With all the big decisions,
make them with the heart.

00:04:39.699 --> 00:04:41.790
So the question of the
day today is I'm curious,

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:44.540
who has given you the best advice

00:04:45.499 --> 00:04:47.769
for your business, and what was it?

00:04:47.769 --> 00:04:48.753
Leave it in the comments below.

00:04:48.753 --> 00:04:50.271
I'm super curious to find out.

00:04:50.271 --> 00:04:52.504
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Stefan Patak.

00:04:52.504 --> 00:04:53.968
Thank you so much, man, for picking up

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:55.849
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:04:55.849 --> 00:04:57.493
It really, really,
really means a lot to me,

00:04:57.493 --> 00:04:59.905
and I hope that you're enjoying the read.

00:04:59.905 --> 00:05:01.144
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:05:01.144 --> 00:05:02.290
I believe in you.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:05.196
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself,

00:05:05.196 --> 00:05:07.463
and whatever your one word is.

00:05:07.463 --> 00:05:09.714
Much love, I'll see you
guys again tomorrow morning

00:05:09.714 --> 00:05:12.933
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:05:12.933 --> 00:05:15.541
♫ I wake up every morning

00:05:15.541 --> 00:05:18.958
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:05:22.832 --> 00:05:25.847
- The only time in the last
couple of years that I knew,

00:05:25.847 --> 00:05:27.654
as soon as we finished a song,

00:05:27.654 --> 00:05:29.435
that it was sort of a, like,

00:05:29.435 --> 00:05:31.505
I hate to say game changer,

00:05:31.505 --> 00:05:35.412
but that it was sort of a
next level situation was

00:05:35.412 --> 00:05:37.648
when I finished Shake It Off.

00:05:37.648 --> 00:05:40.148
But I wanted to be sure, so I,

00:05:41.404 --> 00:05:43.508
that was the very end of
the recording process.

00:05:43.508 --> 00:05:45.132
I finished Shake It Off and I knew

00:05:45.132 --> 00:05:46.531
I was done with the record,

00:05:46.531 --> 00:05:48.910
and I flew back to Nashville,

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.012
had a bunch of label people who I trust,

00:05:51.012 --> 00:05:53.141
and a bunch of management who I trust,

00:05:53.141 --> 00:05:56.177
and my mom and dad sit in
my parents' living room,

00:05:56.177 --> 00:05:57.775
and I played them the full record,

00:05:57.775 --> 00:06:00.096
and I didn't tell them anything about

00:06:00.096 --> 00:06:02.286
how I thought I had
written the first single.

00:06:02.286 --> 00:06:03.808
I didn't tell them anything like,

00:06:03.808 --> 00:06:06.058
"You got to listen, like,
listen for track eight.

00:06:06.058 --> 00:06:08.972
"Shake It Off is the
one, I'm telling you."

00:06:08.972 --> 00:06:11.450
But when that song came
on and halfway through,

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:15.058
all of them look at me
and go, "This is the one,"

00:06:15.058 --> 00:06:17.441
it was such a validating feeling because

00:06:17.441 --> 00:06:20.268
I thought I knew, and
I was so sure I knew,

00:06:20.268 --> 00:06:23.101
and then it turned out I did know.

